##EXP 10

Aim:
To implement synchronized multithreading in Java using synchronization 
and inter-thread communication.


Procedure:
Create a shared Buffer class with synchronized produce() and consume() methods.
Use wait() and notify() for communication between threads.
Create Producer and Consumer classes to produce and consume data.
Start both threads and display the produced and consumed values.


Result:
Thus, the Java program using synchronization and inter-thread
communication was successfully executed.


##program 10

class Buffer {
    int data;
    boolean available = false;

    synchronized void produce(int x) throws Exception {
        while (available) wait();
        data = x;
        System.out.println("Produced: " + data);
        available = true;
        notify();
    }

    synchronized void consume() throws Exception {
        while (!available) wait();
        System.out.println("Consumed: " + data);
        available = false;
        notify();
    }
}

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Buffer b = new Buffer();

        Thread p = new Thread(() -> {
            try {
                for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
                    b.produce(i);
            } catch (Exception e) {}
        });

        Thread c = new Thread(() -> {
            try {
                for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
                    b.consume();
            } catch (Exception e) {}
        });

        p.start();
        c.start();
    }
}


