## exp 13

Aim:
To implement customized sorting in Java using
Comparable and Comparator interfaces.


Procedure:
Create a Student class with roll number and name implementing Comparable.
Override the compareTo() method to sort by roll number.
Create a NameComparator class implementing Comparator to sort by name.
Use Collections.sort() to display the sorted student details.


Result:
Thus, the Java program using Comparable and Comparator 
interfaces was successfully executed.


## program 13

import java.util.*;

class Student implements Comparable<Student> {
    int roll;
    String name;

    Student(int r, String n) {
        roll = r;
        name = n;
    }

    public int compareTo(Student s) {
        return roll - s.roll;
    }

    public String toString() {
        return roll + " " + name;
    }
}

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayList<Student> list = new ArrayList<>();

        list.add(new Student(103, "Ravi"));
        list.add(new Student(101, "Arun"));
        list.add(new Student(102, "Gokul"));

        Collections.sort(list);
        System.out.println("By Roll: " + list);

        list.sort((a, b) -> a.name.compareTo(b.name));
        System.out.println("By Name: " + list);
    }
}

